      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_80506ea142843f96bb5ae80f0d33182c09325ccd57dd07c930481edccbb0bb07",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A layered interface carries analytic zero control to a discrete prime witness: positivity and growth bounds exclude zeros near one, contour displacement converts zero-free width into a quantitative prime-counting estimate, finite verification can be spliced with a tail region for effective constants, and a positive theta increment certifies that some prime occurs.",
